SM(285,{"n":"Exodus 9-10","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Exodus 9-10.mp3","d":2206.3,"s":[[0.24,"Come and study the Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.96,"Father Stephen holds a PhD in biblical studies, and it's an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.64,"Chapter 9. And the Lord said to Moses, Go to Pharaoh and you shall say to him, Thus says the Lord God of the Hebrews, let my people go, so they may serve me."],[33.12,"But if you refuse to let them go and still hold them, behold, the hand of the Lord will be on your cattle in the fields, on the horses, the donkeys, the camels, the oxen, and the sheep."],[42.24,"A very severe pestilence."],[44.88,"Then I will make a clear distinction between the cattle of Israel, the cattle of Egypt, so nothing shall die of all that belongs to the children of Israel."],[52.48,"So he says, Okay, got another chance."],[56.56,"Let them go."],[57.44,"If not, I'm sending a disease on your animals."],[59.36,"I'm gonna wipe out your animals"],[65.0,"And just to make it clear what's going on, none of the animals that belong to the Israelites are gonna die, just yours."],[75.0,"So that's the it's a pestilence."],[76.76,"They're gonna get sick and they're gonna die."],[78.68,"Why is that so important?"],[80.44,"Well, if they die sick, you can't eat them."],[84.84,"And you can't use the leather, and you can't write, they're gonna die of some horrible disease."],[91.32,"You can't even make secondary use of your dead cattle and stuff."],[99.08,"Verse 5 saying, Then God appointed a time, saying, Tomorrow the Lord will do this in the land."],[104.36,"If you don't let him go, tomorrow this is gonna happen"],[105.22,"So he gives him a day warning."],[111.14,"So the Lord did this thing on the next day, and all the cattle of the Egyptians died."],[115.78,"But of the cattle of the children of Israel, not one died."],[119.86,"Then Pharaoh said, and indeed, not even one among the cattle of the Israelites was dead."],[124.9,"But the heart of Pharaoh was hardened, and he did not let the people go."],[128.74,"Still no dice."],[130.39,"Things are getting pretty bad in Egypt now at this point."],[134.0,"So you not only have all the death and decay and stuff, but now you've got all these animals, pack animals, herd animals, milk cattle."],[143.78,"Any animals anybody might have eaten dead."],[147.87,"Joe Egyptian must be pretty upset at this point."],[152.91,"He doesn't get to vote, though."],[155.23,"Yeah. They wouldn't even be able to offer sacrifices either."],[160.37,"No, you no sacrificial animals."],[162.37,"Yeah. Which is probably connected back to that bit about the abomination of the Egyptians."],[167.41,"Yeah. That was like sacrifices."],[169.89,"Yeah. Verse 8."],[172.93,"Yeah, so there is an element of that."],[174.45,"There's an element of you're not gonna let my people go worship their God?"],[177.41,"Okay okay. Good luck worshiping yours."],[179.49,"Verse 8. So the Lord said to Moses and Aaron, take for yourselves handfuls of ashes from a furnace."],[186.13,"And let Moses scatter it toward heaven in the sight of Pharaoh, and let it become dust in all in the all land the. land of Egypt, and it will cause boils to break out sores on man and beast throughout of Egypt"],[198.09,"So you notice also we're escalating."],[202.49,"From its hard to find water."],[203.77,"Oh no, those were all the cattle and pack animals."],[206.49,"This is animals, the any animal."],[209.99,"Cats, dogs, and the frogs that are still around."],[214.79,"Yeah. Um, and all the humans."],[218.88,"But you don't see how this is escalating."],[221.06,"We've gone from like nuisance and irritant."],[223.96,"We went from like lice to like biting flies, seven days in a water to dead animals, to now people having giant boils and skin disease."],[234.2,"It's getting worse and worse"],[239.49,"Now you have to imagine, right again, remember what's Pharaoh's job?"],[244.85,"Preserve the good order of Egypt."],[246.53,"Egypt is chaos now."],[249.91,"This is chaos and destruction."],[252.43,"I mentioned that back in the 16th century, a date which pretty much no one has for the Exodus, we do have this account."],[260.83,"We have this account, it's very poetic."],[264.21,"But there is this poetic account for this Egyptian talking about how disaster had fallen upon Egypt and it was dark in the middle of the day, and everything was dead, and all of the right, and so. like, that's not proof of anything, because of course, maybe he's just being poetic"],[281.69,"There were certainly other bad times in the history of Egypt."],[284.97,"We can't be, but this term is very redolent of this."],[288.17,"So we can at least say from that."],[290.55,"When when this Egyptian wrote that, he was like, the gods are all angry at us and are out to destroy us."],[297.85,"So it sort of shows us how the Egyptians would interpret that."],[303.69,"Yeah, how they would understand what was happening."],[305.85,"So they took ashes from the furnace and stood before Pharaoh, and Moses scattered them toward heaven, and they caused boils to break out in sores on man and beast."],[314.89,"Now the sorcerers could not stand before Moses because of the sores, for the sores were on the sorcerers in all the land of Egypt."],[321.57,"So they can't even show up to say or do anything, because they're afflicted now with the boils and the Pharaoh is too."],[331.25,"Yeah. But the Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart, and he did not heed them, as the Lord said to Moses."],[337.17,"Then the Lord said to Moses, Rise early in the morning and stand before Pharaoh, and say to him, Thus says the Lord God of the Hebrews, let my people go so they may serve me."],[347.17,"For at this time I will send all my plagues into your very heart, and on your servants and your people, that you may know there is not another such as I in all the earth."],[359.01,"Again, there's not another such as I in all the earth."],[364.77,"Different category. Than the quote unquote gods you're used to dealing with"],[372.46,"And he's saying this is about to escalate a lot."],[379.1,"This is about to get way worse."],[381.5,"You're being warned."],[383.1,"Verse 15, for now I will stretch forth my hand and smite you and kill your people, and you will be cut off from the earth."],[389.1,"That's pretty direct."],[391.56,"Not nuisance, not sick, not sores."],[395.8,"People are gonna die now."],[398.04,"But for this very reason, were you preserved, that I might display in you my strength, and that my name might be declared in all the earth."],[405.48,"So, what's he saying there?"],[406.84,"For this reason you are preserved."],[408.68,"This is a sorry Calvinist, because our Calvinist friends will point to where St"],[413.84,"Paul quotes us and they'll say, aha, see, God predestined all this to happen."],[418.0,"Pharaoh didn't have a choice, even though it seems like he's had a whole bunch of choices."],[423.12,"He didn't have a choice, God made him do this to display his glory."],[426.8,"But that's not what it says."],[428.8,"It's not actually what it says."],[430.16,"This is for this reason you are preserved."],[434.16,"What does that mean?"],[437.12,"This is why God is doing this now."],[440.9,"Because God could have, you know, as soon as he started murdering babies, God could have just, you know, killed him."],[449.86,"Or killed all the Egyptians."],[451.22,"Or killed all the Egyptians."],[452.34,"Or just killed Pharaoh."],[453.16,"Just had Pharaoh drop dead."],[453.48,"He was eaten by worms and died"],[454.56,"That happened to Herod."],[455.44,"Remember, Herod murdered all those babies, and then what happened?"],[462.09,"So this is God saying, God is saying, why does God allow something like this to happen?"],[469.37,"Why does he allow a man like this to have this much power in the world?"],[473.61,"And do so much evil with it."],[477.22,"Why doesn't God do something about that?"],[481.3,"This is the answer to that."],[482.9,"This is, oh, he's going to do something about that."],[486.6,"But he's doing something about that when the time is right."],[492.62,"When the time is right."],[493.9,"He's doing something about Pharaoh, but he's doing it in the eyes of the whole world."],[499.94,"To reveal who he is."],[503.3,"Because if Pharaoh is going to harden his heart and Pharaoh is going to refuse to turn from evil and turn from idolatry and turn from all these things and embrace God, there are a bunch of Egyptians who will."],[517.78,"There's some people in other parts of the world who will."],[524.58,"And they matter just as much as Pharaoh does."],[526.9,"Yes. rescue it"],[528.34,"Yes. And so this is the reason God has let this continue."],[538.18,"Let all this happen is in preparation for this. moment where he is going to bring good out of it"],[545.42,"He is going to bring good out of that evil."],[549.34,"Because the perspective, sorry, Calvinists, of the Torah is not that God punishes evil."],[557.66,"It's not that he punishes evil or that he punishes sin."],[561.74,"It's that, as we saw with like Joseph, that God brings good out of human evil."],[567.26,"He brings good out of it."],[570.46,"He loves humans, all of them."],[575.39,"And he wants them to turn and find salvation."],[580.51,"And if God, every time someone did evil, cut them down, we'd all be in a lot of trouble."],[584.91,"That wouldn't serve God's purpose"],[590.85,"God doesn't desire the death of a wicked man, but that he turn and live."],[594.77,"And if Pharaoh won't turn and live, again, a bunch of Egyptians will."],[600.21,"And a bunch of people in other countries who hear about this will."],[603.65,"And a bunch of Israelites will."],[606.13,"And so he's allowed Pharaoh to remain in power."],[610.21,"He's allowed Pharaoh to continue to live."],[615.81,"He's been patient with him."],[616.85,"He's been generous until now."],[619.57,"And now he's telling Pharaoh in advance, my generosity and my patience is about done."],[628.02,"And now there's going to be a reckoning."],[628.9,"be There's gonna a reckoning."],[631.24,"Because that's what that's what we're gonna get from the whole scriptures."],[635.88,"Whole scripture starting in the Torah is that God is patient and forbearing to a point."],[645.32,"And then that point comes, and there's a reckoning."],[649.08,"That's true for individual people, that's true for nations, and people groups."],[656.46,"That's true for rulers."],[658.44,"But there's a point that's reached, and there's different languages that's used."],[661.32,"The cup of iniquity is full."],[664.09,"Or different types of language for that."],[666.49,"But that goes all the way to the New Testament."],[668.17,"We saw St."],[668.81,"Peter saying that."],[671.65,"Why does it seem like it's taking so long for Christ to return?"],[675.01,"Does God not care about all the evil things that are happening?"],[678.21,"And the way his people are suffering."],[680.45,"Not at all."],[681.33,"God is being patient so that there's more time for people to repent and turn and live."],[686.77,"But eventually it's sort of like there's scales."],[689.66,"And eventually the victims and the people being hurt and the people being sinned against who are crying out to God, eventually that outweighs God's patience and kindness toward the evildoer."],[702.3,"And then that reckoning happens."],[704.8,"And Herod's reckoning was getting eaten by worms."],[708.2,"We're seeing Pharaoh's reckoning play out"],[712.07,"Because he refuses."],[713.67,"But we're also seeing again and again these opportunities for him, for the Egyptians, for everyone in the world to see this and turn and change and repent."],[723.63,"Isn't there also significance in this happening to the sovereign of the most powerful nation?"],[731.12,"It's not just that the Egyptians are gonna know everything."],[733.92,"The whole world's gonna know because this is Egypt, yes."],[737.12,"This isn't happening off in some corner of the world that nobody's heard of."],[741.44,"This is what everybody knows is this powerful and ancient civilization."],[746.72,"Verse 17, as yet you exalt yourself against my people, and that you will not let them go."],[756.32,"You're still full of yourself."],[759.97,"Behold, tomorrow, about this time I will cause very heavy hail to rain down, such as has not been in Egypt since its founding until now."],[771.01,"A few thousand years."],[773.22,"This is, you know, in recorded history."],[775.62,"I'm about to do something worse than you've ever seen in recorded history."],[779.86,"Therefore, hurry now and gather your cattle and all you have in the fields, for the hail shall come down on every man and animal found in the fields, and whatever is not brought home shall die."],[790.42,"So he not only warns in advance, he says, Here's what to do."],[796.5,"So anybody who believes him, that this is true."],[801.21,"So this is. more than just I'm not going to send it on Goshen"],[806.99,"This is, hey, anyone who hears this, that shift's starting to happen too."],[811.87,"We're going to see that play out over the course of these last few plagues."],[815.79,"Any Egyptian who hears about this and believes it can go and get ever get everyone inside, get everything inside, and protect themselves."],[825.0,"Thus he who feared the word of the Lord among the servants of Pharaoh gathered his cattle into the houses, but he who did not regard the word of the Lord left his servants and cattle in the fields."],[835.16,"Verse 22: Then the Lord said to Moses, Stretch out your hand toward heaven, and there shall be hail in all the land of Egypt, both on man and cattle and on every herb of the field throughout the land of Egypt."],[846.96,"So Moses stretched out his rod toward heaven, and the Lord sent thunder and hail, and fire darted to the ground."],[853.92,"Thus the Lord rained hail on the land of Egypt."],[857.6,"So this may be another Father Stephen ruins your Sunday school."],[860.88,"But the fire part is lightning."],[863.6,"And Egypt is a country with almost no rain."],[866.96,"Yes. They didn't even they called rain Niles in the sky."],[871.44,"Yeah. This is thunder, lightning, massive hailstones."],[877.6,"Massive hailstorm. But yes, they didn't have a concept of electricity."],[881.52,"So they referred to lightning as fire from heaven."],[884.08,"That's why it talks about fire darting to the ground."],[888.58,"That's lightning. And that makes sense."],[890.78,"Again, if you're looking at it, the place where lightning hits catches on fire."],[897.8,"So, yeah, that's that makes sense."],[901.48,"Verse 24, this hail and the fire mingled with it were so very heavy, there was none like it in all the land of Egypt since it became a nation."],[909.88,"And throughout the whole land of Egypt, it struck both man and cattle and every herb of the field and broke every tree of the field."],[916.6,"Only in the land of Goshen, where the children of Israel were, there was no hail."],[922.84,"So we still have that split made, but we also, the Egyptians, this time, got some extra warning."],[929.7,"If they believed."],[932.58,"Verse 27. Then Pharaoh said sent and called for Moses and Aaron and to them, I have sinned this time."],[934.18,"The Lord is righteous"],[940.06,"My people and I are ungodly."],[942.92,"He said, Okay, I'm in the wrong this time."],[946.44,"Notice that. This time."],[949.4,"The other ones know, but but this time I'm in the wrong."],[953.0,"Why would he be in the wrong?"],[954.12,"I think he was in the wrong this time."],[956.04,"Because he told him to bring everyone inside."],[958.36,"I should have listened to you and brought everyone inside."],[960.92,"My bad. Not getting it at all still."],[965.81,"Not able to acknowledge even acknowledge any of what's happening."],[969.65,"Therefore, pray for me to the Lord and let him cause the thunderings of God to cease, and the hail and fire, for I will let you go and you shall stay no longer."],[979.93,"So Moses said to him, As soon as I have gone out of the city, I will spread out my hands to the Lord."],[984.41,"The thunder will cease, there will be no more hail and rain, that you may know the earth is the Lord's."],[989.61,"Now the word that's translated earth there can also mean land."],[993.31,"And I think that's actually more pointedly the meaning."],[996.59,"The land is in the land of Egypt."],[1000.11,"The whole thing belongs to Yahweh, not. I know you will yet fear the Lord"],[1010.41,"So again, Moses is dumb."],[1012.01,"It's like I know it's gonna happen."],[1013.29,"I'm gonna go out there, I'm gonna pray."],[1015.21,"The storm's gonna stop, but you don't really get it, and you're not gonna."],[1022.1,"Fool me once."],[1025.54,"Now the flax and the barley were struck, for the barley was ripe and the flax was beginning to seed."],[1031.06,"But as for the wheat and the rye, they were not struck, for they were late crops."],[1034.82,"So on top of everything else, the storm kills all the crops that were planted at the time that this happened."],[1044.42,"So now they're gonna have food problems in Egypt to boot, on top of everything else, and on top of all the dead people."],[1051.7,"So Moses went out from the city from Pharaoh and spread out his hands to the Lord."],[1055.7,"Then the thunder and the hail ceased, and the rain was not poured on the earth."],[1059.62,"Thus, when Pharaoh saw that the rain, the hail, and the thunder ceased, he sinned yet more, and he hardened his heart and the heart of his servants."],[1068.14,"So the heart of Pharaoh was hardened, neither would he let the children of Israel go, as the Lord said to Moses."],[1075.5,"So again, just like Moses said, because God told him."],[1080.62,"Because he could see pat he has pattern recognition skills."],[1083.96,"He knew that Pharaoh was not had not really changed."],[1089.4,"Chapter ten. Now the Lord said to Moses, Go into Pharaoh, for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants, that these signs may come upon them, and that you may tell in the hearing of your children and your children's children, in how many things I mocked the Egyptians, and my wonders I wrought among them, and you shall know I am the Lord."],[1109.32,"So notice something here."],[1110.44,"Again, another sorry Calvinist."],[1112.88,"People get really hung up on this."],[1114.88,"God hardened Pharaoh's heart and the heart of his servants."],[1118.48,"We just read two verses ago that Pharaoh hardened his sin more and hardened his own heart."],[1123.68,"And that Pharaoh hardened the hearts of his servants."],[1126.72,"Do you see that was the actual language there?"],[1128.96,"Pharaoh hardened the hearts of his servants."],[1131.45,"So if you want to read this as God somehow coming in and making Pharaoh's heart hard, you have to suppose that Pharaoh had the power to go into his servants' hearts and harden them."],[1146.81,"How he would do that, I don't know."],[1148.57,"Maybe hypnosis. So that doesn't work."],[1153.28,"In in terms of an explanation."],[1154.16,"of The hardening the heart signifies what?"],[1155.4,"But remember what the hardening of the heart signifies."],[1162.58,"That's weighed down by evil, sin, wickedness."],[1166.96,"So when it says God hardened his or Pharaoh hardened his servants' hearts, it's talking about recognition of sin."],[1176.24,"God looks at his heart and sees it is full of sin."],[1179.04,"It doesn't say God made him sin, because we just said Pharaoh did that."],[1184.36,"So the fact that God is involved here, what is essentially saying is God's not like forgiving him."],[1192.04,"So remember, what did he say to Pharaoh right before this last plague?"],[1196.36,"He said, yeah, he said. up to this point, I've been patient"],[1202.48,"Up to this point, I've been bearing with you, but that's about to change."],[1207.49,"St. Paul is going to say something very similar to this in Athens in Acts 17."],[1213.49,"He's going to say, up until now, God has not reckoned, you people out here in the nations, you don't know any better."],[1221.73,"God hasn't been reckoning your sins against you."],[1225.62,"He's been patient with you."],[1227.44,"He's been letting you be."],[1228.72,"He hasn't been punishing you for all this stuff you've been doing."],[1232.08,"But now the time is coming when that's going to happen."],[1235.2,"And so you need to repent."],[1237.04,"That's the same thing."],[1238.4,"This is where St."],[1239.76,"Paul is getting it."],[1241.48,"This is what's being said to Pharaoh."],[1243.4,"Up until that plague, God had been being patient, but now that's done."],[1252.84,"And so now Pharaoh's sins, his evil, his wickedness is being held against him."],[1258.44,"He's going to be held to account for it."],[1262.52,"God's not going to lighten his heart by forgiving him, by being patient anymore, by bearing with him anymore."],[1270.6,"Now the reckoning has begun here in these final plagues."],[1274.12,"And he says, and you will tell in the hearing of your children and your children's children, and your children's children's children, all the way down to today, in the year 2024, as we read this."],[1284.46,"Of what happened. to the Egyptians"],[1286.74,"Verse 3 So Moses and Aaron came into Pharaoh and said to him, Thus says the Lord, God of the Hebrews, how long will you refuse to humble yourself before me?"],[1299.46,"Notice that this is the first time we've heard that language."],[1302.34,"It's a shift."],[1303.78,"Previous plague it was you exalt yourself against my people."],[1307.86,"You think you're better than my people."],[1310.98,"Pharaoh would have said, Of course I'm better than your people, they're slaves."],[1314.78,"Now it's right."],[1317.58,"Why won't you humble yourself before me?"],[1321.42,"Pharaoh doesn't humble himself before anybody."],[1325.76,"Maybe the sun god, who's supposed to be his father."],[1328.4,"Yeah, exactly, maybe"],[1329.48,"Maybe. But not the god of a bunch of slaves."],[1338.17,"Let my people go so they may serve me."],[1340.73,"Or else, if you refuse to let my people go, behold, tomorrow I will bring an abundance of locusts into your territory."],[1346.97,"And they shall cover the face of the earth, so no one will be able to see the earth, and they will eat the residue of what is left of the land's abundance which remains to you from the hail."],[1357.45,"They shall eat every tree which grows up for you out of the field."],[1361.13,"You shall fill your houses, the houses of all your servants, and the houses of all the Egyptians, which neither your fathers nor their forefathers saw since the day they were on the earth to this day."],[1371.53,"So this is even."],[1372.57,"This is since there have been humans"],[1372.93,"Remember the last one was since Egypt became a nation?"],[1380.75,"Since there have been humans, they have not seen this."],[1383.23,"So Moses turned and went out from Pharaoh."],[1385.07,"Now you would think, since every other warning he's gotten has come and come true."],[1390.29,"Exactly as said."],[1391.73,"And since this warning is literally these locusts are going to come and devour every bit of food."],[1398.45,"Food left in your entire nation, so you will have nothing to eat."],[1404.62,"That he would figure, oh, that's yeah, that's probably gonna happen tomorrow."],[1408.86,"I can't eat gold, bro."],[1411.74,"But wait, but what would he have to do to acknowledge that?"],[1416.02,"He'd have to humble himself."],[1419.22,"He'd have to admit that the god of these slaves is more powerful than him, has bested him."],[1427.2,"And that requires too much, as we've said a couple of times today."],[1431.36,"Then Pharaoh's servant said to him, How long shall this man be a snare to us?"],[1435.44,"Let the men go so they may serve their God."],[1437.92,"Do you not yet know Egypt is destroyed?"],[1440.66,"So his own advisors are saying to him, pro, like if you bet outside, the nation is in ruins."],[1448.5,"Just let these people go."],[1450.5,"We don't even like them."],[1452.4,"Just let them go, man."],[1455.12,"So Moses and Aaron were brought again to Pharaoh."],[1457.86,"So they're like, go and get the no, come back, come back, come back."],[1459.3,"And he said to them, Go serve the Lord your God"],[1465.34,"But who are the ones going?"],[1469.1,"We're negotiating again."],[1470.75,"We're negotiating. Moses replied, We will go with our young and old, with our sons and daughters, with our sheep and oxen, for we must hold a feast to the Lord."],[1478.27,"Then he said to them, Let the Lord be with you when I let you and your little ones go, but not your belongings."],[1485.07,"For evil lies before you."],[1487.39,"Not so, but let the men go and serve God, for that is what you desired."],[1492.27,"Then they were driven out from Pharaoh's presence."],[1494.75,"So he doesn't really offer a compromise."],[1497.79,"He says, Here's what we'll do."],[1500.03,"Your men could go out."],[1502.91,"Women, children, all your belongings, they stay here"],[1508.31,"And then no further negotiations."],[1511.59,"Now get out of here."],[1512.87,"Verse 12 And the Lord said to Moses, Stretch out your hand over the land of Egypt, and let the locusts come upon the land of Egypt and eat every herb of the land, everything the hail left."],[1522.31,"So Moses stretched out his rod toward heaven, and the Lord brought a south wind on the land all that day and night."],[1527.75,"When it was morning, the south wind brought the locusts, and the locusts went up over all the land of Egypt and rested in very great abundance in all the territory of Egypt."],[1536.23,"Previously there were no such locusts as they, nor shall there be such after them."],[1541.67,"So never have been, never will be a swarm of locusts like this."],[1545.11,"For they covered the face of the land, and the land was wasted."],[1547.83,"They ate every herb of the land. and all the fruit of the trees left by the hail"],[1551.71,"There remained nothing green on the trees or on the plants of the field throughout all the land of Egypt."],[1556.83,"Then Pharaoh called for Moses and Aaron in haste and said, I have sinned against the Lord your God and against you."],[1564.33,"Oh, I really blew it this time."],[1566.97,"There's no food."],[1568.57,"Now therefore, pardon my sin yet this time."],[1572.41,"Oh, please forgive me, Moses."],[1576.09,"And pray to the Lord your God that he take away from me this death."],[1581.53,"So Moses went out from Pharaoh and prayed to God."],[1583.93,"Then the Lord brought in from the opposite direction a strong wind from the sea, which took the locusts away and blew them into the Red Sea."],[1591.29,"There remained not one locust in all the territory of Egypt."],[1594.53,"But the Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart and he did not let the children of Israel go."],[1599.17,"So notice why does it say hear that the Lord hardened his heart?"],[1603.17,"Because what did he ask?"],[1604.93,"Pardon my sin."],[1607.01,"So God did not pardon him."],[1608.53,"God did not."],[1609.73,"Because he still did not let the people go."],[1613.07,"He did not let the people go."],[1614.99,"He didn't actually repent."],[1617.63,"Repentance is not feeling bad."],[1621.47,"Repentance is not disliking the consequences of your sin."],[1627.25,"And wanting to get out of them."],[1629.49,"And wanting to get off the hook for what you did."],[1633.67,"Repentance is actually changing."],[1638.11,"How you think and how you act and what you do and acting upon it."],[1644.19,"So Pharaoh really repenting."],[1646.91,"It's not that God wouldn't forgive his sin."],[1651.07,"God would forgive his sin if he repented."],[1653.63,"But what would be the sign that he had repented?"],[1655.95,"He would have let them go."],[1657.55,"And so saying, gosh, I feel bad."],[1659.55,"Yeah, I'm in the wrong."],[1661.63,"Please forgive me."],[1663.71,"You know, and pray and get rid of these locusts."],[1666.11,"That's not repenting."],[1667.63,"It's not repenting."],[1669.76,"And let me add, even though this was somewhat controversial when I've said it in the past, feeling bad is not repenting."],[1676.02,"I dare say, and I know this will shock any millennials here."],[1679.62,"God cares about what you do"],[1680.3,"God doesn't really care how you feel."],[1685.66,"Okay? If you do the wrong thing and feel bad about it, that doesn't matter."],[1689.66,"You still did the wrong thing."],[1691.1,"If you do the right thing and your heart's not in it, you still did the right thing."],[1695.84,"There's a parable about this."],[1698.24,"Remember, Christ tells the parable about the two sons."],[1702.48,"Father comes to them and says, hey, because the first one says, hey, go work in the vineyard."],[1707.12,"Says, buzz off, dad."],[1709.66,"And then later he feels bad about it."],[1712.88,"But it's not that he feels bad about it."],[1714.72,"It's not that he goes and asks his dad to forgive him for being rude."],[1718.08,"It's he goes out and he works in the vineyard."],[1721.93,"He goes to the other son, he says, son, go work in the vineyard."],[1725.17,"Son says, Yeah, I'm on it, and then doesn't do it."],[1728.45,"He's very polite and nice to his father."],[1731.25,"But he didn't do it."],[1732.77,"He didn't do what his father wanted."],[1735.06,"So God doesn't want you to sit around feeling bad about your sin, especially not after you confessed it."],[1741.64,"He wants you to come and confess it, and then he wants you to work to change and do better."],[1746.2,"And to fix what you broke."],[1748.22,"And to try and repair the damage you've done."],[1750.86,"That's what he wants you to do."],[1752.14,"That's what repentance is."],[1754.4,"And even if you do that begrudgingly, I mean that's not ideal."],[1758.85,"But even if you do it begrudgingly, at least you're doing it."],[1761.83,"At least you're doing it."],[1762.87,"There's this whole idea in our society that you shouldn't do something if your heart's not in it."],[1768.67,"That's why we have the divorce rate we have in our society."],[1773.07,"Because people think it's better, to leave their family because their heart's not in it anymore."],[1780.65,"Than to stay and do the right thing even though their heart's not in it and they don't feel like it."],[1786.09,"Which is a fundamental breakdown in what morality has been in the entire history of humanity."],[1795.05,"The entire history of humanity, morality, ethics, whatever we want to call it, has been about doing the right thing."],[1802.14,"Not gratifying our own desires."],[1804.94,"Not doing what we feel like."],[1806.72,"But now. it's no, you need to follow your heart"],[1812.44,"You need to do what feels right."],[1814.92,"Well, if you follow your heart, it's liable to end up really hard."],[1818.84,"And even though it's not going to be weighed in front of an alligator god."],[1824.16,"It's not going to do well for you on the actual day of judgment to stand before Christ and say, Well, you know, I pursued happiness."],[1832.88,"When he asked why you did the things you did and hurt the people you hurt."],[1836.88,"Plague number nine."],[1838.8,"Notice what comes here in plague number nine."],[1841.68,"You can see the subheading."],[1843.92,"Remember who the king of the gods is for the Egyptians."],[1846.8,"The sun god."],[1847.64,"Ray, sun god."],[1849.04,"Verse 21: Then the Lord said to Moses, Stretch out your hand. toward heaven, and let there be darkness over the land of Egypt, a darkness that may be felt"],[1857.0,"So Moses stretched out his hand toward heaven, and there was thick darkness in all the land of Egypt for three days."],[1862.84,"No one saw his brother for three days, nor did anyone rise from his bed for three days."],[1867.88,"But all the children of Israel had light in their dwellings."],[1870.92,"Now notice what it says, had light in their dwellings."],[1873.88,"So this isn't just no sun for three days."],[1878.04,"This is they can't light a fire."],[1881.46,"They can't start a fire, they can't light a candle, they can't light a lamp."],[1886.39,"Pitch black. Except in Goshen."],[1889.8,"Pitch black. So this obviously goes right in the face of Ray, the sun god."],[1894.28,"god Who's supposed to be their king of thes?"],[1894.44,"Oops He can't get through this darkness that that Yahweh is causing."],[1901.82,"I don't know."],[1903.34,"Probably maybe everybody's had this."],[1905.02,"The first time I had I had the experience of actual like pitch black was on a camping trip once where we were out in the desert, because I grew up in California, and so there's no ambient light."],[1919.42,"We're way out in the desert camping, and everybody turned off all their flashlights."],[1924.7,"So that it was literally."],[1926.46,"I remember putting my hand like two inches from my face, and I could not see my hand."],[1931.34,"Like I could not, like it was just nothing."],[1934.75,"That's the kind of darkness we're talking about here."],[1938.43,"For three days"],[1939.27,"Fumbling around in the dark."],[1943.96,"Until you think about it that way, it doesn't seem like an escalation."],[1947.93,"But imagine that."],[1950.35,"Imagine being completely blind."],[1952.83,"Everyone in your city is completely blind for three days."],[1957.23,"There's no work, no food, no one can see no water."],[1960.83,"Verse 24, then Pharaoh called to Moses and said, Go serve the Lord your God."],[1965.15,"Only let your sheep and oxen be kept back."],[1967.95,"Let your belongings also go with you."],[1970.35,"He's still trying to negotiate."],[1972.83,"What does that show?"],[1973.71,"He still doesn't get it."],[1975.39,"He's still putting himself on some kind of par with Yahweh, the God of Israel."],[1980.91,"Where he doesn't have to obey."],[1981.09,"Where he can negotiate."],[1985.89,"Pharaoh doesn't obey anybody."],[1989.02,"But Moses said, No, but you must give us whole burnt offerings and sacrifices that we may sacrifice to the Lord our God."],[1995.1,"Thus our cattle shall go with us, not a hoof shall be left behind, for we must take some of them to serve the Lord our God."],[2001.66,"And even we do not know in what manner we shall serve the Lord our God until we arrive there."],[2005.58,"So he's saying, We've got to take the animals, we have to sacrifice."],[2007.74,"The whole point is we're going there to worship."],[2009.5,"And worship is sacrifice in the ancient world."],[2013.34,"Verse 27, but the Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart, he would not let them go."],[2017.02,"Then Pharaoh said to him, Depart from me, take heed for yourself that you see my face no more, for in the day you see my face you shall die."],[2024.94,"That's a threat"],[2025.46,"So Moses said, You have spoken well, I will never see your face again."],[2030.26,"So how does Pharaoh respond?"],[2032.02,"Okay, take your animals."],[2034.18,"Nope, get away from me."],[2036.34,"Next time I see you, I'm gonna kill you."],[2038.82,"That ain't repentance."],[2041.67,"That ain't repentance."],[2043.43,"And so, again, no forgiveness."],[2048.37,"No forgiveness. And so Pharaoh has pushed this."],[2053.25,"We're gonna end here, but he's pushed this up to the point of what we're gonna talk about next time, which is gonna be true horror."],[2062.05,"This wasn't. Not compared to what's gonna happen."],[2067.71,"He's pushed it here"],[2071.99,"Because he simply cannot make that mental turn."],[2079.35,"That there's someone or something in the universe that I have to obey."],[2087.11,"Even his advisors can see it now."],[2090.71,"Like, you know?"],[2093.99,"But it's not that he can't see it, it's that he can't accept that."],[2099.19,"Because it would require too much of him."],[2102.97,"More than he's able and willing to do in terms of who he is, his world, his whole cosmology, like his whole sense of the world."],[2111.85,"Stubborn Kind of feels sorry."],[2113.09,"And Egypt. That's but again, why is this coming upon him?"],[2119.57,"Mass murder of infants."],[2121.33,"Well, not just that."],[2122.66,"The enslavement of a whole people group."],[2124.84,"I mean, it's not like he's this just this poor random guy."],[2129.38,"He's done all yeah."],[2130.26,"He's he's done all this evil, and God's been giving him a free ride."],[2135.3,"You know, expect him to bring order, even though he's corrupted it, he's still in that position to bring order."],[2142.64,"He should have, governed justly."],[2146.58,"He could have."],[2147.62,"But he didn't."],[2148.94,"He could have stopped it playing one, you know."],[2150.94,"Yes, yeah, yeah."],[2152.46,"Or even beforehand, before he first time Moses and Aaron showed up."],[2154.62,"And said, let us go sacrifice"],[2158.26,"Yeah. Go into the desert for a couple days, we'll come back."],[2164.34,"He could have said, okay."],[2168.12,"But now he's pushed it to this point."],[2170.68,"And now it's going to get really bad."],[2173.24,"But God is also going to reveal himself in a very powerful way."],[2176.76,"But we will talk more about that when we come back next week."],[2180.28,"So thank you, everybody."],[2183.96,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2191.32,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2196.68,"That's whole counsel at ancientfa.ith.com"]],"o":[{"t":20.64,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 9:1-4 - Plague 5: livestock","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 9</b> - \"Go to Pharaoh\": let my people go <b>so they may serve me</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Refuse → hand of the Lord on <b>cattle</b>: horses, donkeys, camels, oxen, sheep</li><li class=\"d1\">\"very severe <b>pestilence</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Clear distinction</b> between Israel's cattle and Egypt's - nothing of Israel's dies</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Okay, got another chance\" - else <b>\"wipe out your animals\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pestilence = sick and die</li><li class=\"d1\">if they die sick you <b>can't eat</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">can't use the <b>leather</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no <b>secondary use</b> of dead cattle</li></ul>"},{"t":99.08,"lv":3,"h":"9:5-7 - The cattle die","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v5: God appoints a time - <b>\"tomorrow\"</b>; a <b>day's warning</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Next day <b>all Egyptian cattle died</b>; of Israel's <b>not one</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh checks - not even one Israelite animal dead</li><li class=\"d1\">heart <b>hardened</b>, doesn't let people go - \"Still no dice\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Egypt now: death and decay + <b>pack animals, herd animals, milk cattle</b> all dead</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Joe Egyptian must be pretty upset\" - \"doesn't get to vote, though\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Also <b>no sacrificial animals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ties back to the <b>abomination of the Egyptians</b> (sacrifices)</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not gonna let my people worship their God? Good luck worshiping yours\"</li></ul>"},{"t":169.89,"lv":2,"h":"9:8-12 - Plague 6: boils","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v8: handfuls of <b>ashes from a furnace</b>; Moses scatters toward heaven</li><li class=\"d1\">dust over all Egypt → <b>boils, sores</b> on <b>man and beast</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Escalating</b></li><li class=\"d1\">nuisance and irritant: lice, biting flies, 7 days of bad water</li><li class=\"d1\">→ dead animals → <b>people with giant boils</b>, skin disease</li><li class=\"d1\">\"getting worse and worse\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh's job = <b>preserve the good order of Egypt</b> - now <b>chaos and destruction</b></li></ul>"},{"t":252.43,"lv":3,"h":"Egyptian poem of disaster","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Back in the <b>16th century BC</b> - date \"pretty much no one has for the Exodus\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Egyptian account, very <b>poetic</b>: disaster on Egypt, <b>dark in the middle of the day</b>, everything dead</li><li class=\"d1\">not proof of anything - maybe just being poetic; other bad times in Egypt</li><li class=\"d1\">but language <b>\"very redolent\"</b> of this</li><li class=\"d0\">Shows how Egyptians would <b>interpret</b> it: <b>the gods are angry and out to destroy us</b></li></ul>"},{"t":305.85,"lv":3,"h":"Sorcerers afflicted too","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ashes taken, Moses scatters them → boils on man and beast</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Sorcerers could not stand before Moses</b> - sores on them too</li><li class=\"d1\">can't even show up to say or do anything</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh afflicted too</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart</b> - he did not heed, as the Lord said</li></ul>"},{"t":337.17,"lv":2,"h":"9:13-16 - Final warning: \"for this reason you were preserved\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Rise early\"; same message: let my people go</li><li class=\"d0\">This time <b>all my plagues into your very heart</b>, on servants and people</li><li class=\"d1\">that you know <b>none like me in all the earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"different category\" than the quote-unquote gods</li><li class=\"d0\">\"About to <b>escalate a lot</b>\" - \"you're being warned\"</li><li class=\"d0\">v15: I will <b>stretch forth my hand, smite you, kill your people</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not nuisance, not sick, not sores - <b>people are gonna die</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v16: <b>\"for this reason you were preserved\"</b> - display my <b>strength</b>, name declared in all the earth</li></ul>"},{"t":405.48,"lv":3,"h":"Not predestination: why God lets Pharaoh be","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Sorry, <b>Calvinists</b>\" - cite St. Paul quoting this: God predestined it, Pharaoh no choice</li><li class=\"d1\">but he's had a whole bunch of choices; <b>not what it says</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"You are <b>preserved</b>\" - why God is doing this <b>now</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God could have killed him when he started murdering babies - or killed all Egyptians</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh could have dropped dead - <b>eaten by worms</b> like <b>Herod</b>, who also murdered babies</li><li class=\"d0\">Why does God allow a man like this <b>power</b> and so much evil?</li><li class=\"d1\">answer: he <b>is</b> going to do something - <b>when the time is right</b></li><li class=\"d1\">doing it <b>in the eyes of the whole world</b>, to reveal who he is</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh may harden, but <b>Egyptians will turn</b>, people in other parts of the world will</li><li class=\"d1\">\"they matter just as much as Pharaoh does\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Whole world watching: this is the <b>most powerful nation</b>, not some corner nobody's heard of</li></ul>"},{"t":549.34,"lv":3,"h":"God brings good out of evil - then the reckoning","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Torah's perspective: not that God <b>punishes evil</b> or sin</li><li class=\"d1\">as with <b>Joseph</b>: God <b>brings good out of human evil</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>loves all humans</b>, wants them to turn and find salvation</li><li class=\"d0\">If God cut down everyone who did evil, \"we'd all be in a lot of trouble\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"God doesn't desire the death of a wicked man, but that he turn and live\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if Pharaoh won't, Egyptians will, people in other countries, Israelites</li><li class=\"d0\">God has been <b>patient, generous</b> - now: \"my patience is about done\" → <b>reckoning</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Whole of Scripture from the Torah: God <b>patient and forbearing to a point</b></li><li class=\"d1\">then the point comes - for <b>individuals, nations, rulers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"the <b>cup of iniquity</b> is full\"</li><li class=\"d0\">NT: <b>St. Peter</b> - why is Christ's return taking so long?</li><li class=\"d1\">God patient so more <b>repent and live</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>scales</b>: victims' cries eventually outweigh God's patience with the evildoer</li><li class=\"d1\">Herod's reckoning = worms; now <b>Pharaoh's reckoning</b> plays out</li></ul>"},{"t":746.72,"lv":2,"h":"9:17-21 - Plague 7: hail, with instructions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v17: \"still <b>exalt yourself</b> against my people\" - \"still full of yourself\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Tomorrow, <b>very heavy hail</b> - <b>not since Egypt's founding</b> (\"a few thousand years\")</li><li class=\"d1\">\"worse than you've ever seen in recorded history\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hurry</b>: gather cattle and all in the fields - <b>whatever is not brought home shall die</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Warns in advance <b>and</b> says what to do</li><li class=\"d1\">more than \"not on <b>Goshen</b>\" - <b>any Egyptian who believes</b> can bring everyone inside, protect themselves</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>shift starting</b> - plays out over last few plagues</li><li class=\"d0\">v20: he who <b>feared the word of the Lord</b> among Pharaoh's servants → cattle into houses</li><li class=\"d1\">he who didn't regard it left servants and cattle in the fields</li></ul>"},{"t":835.16,"lv":2,"h":"9:22-26 - The hail falls","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Moses stretches out rod → <b>thunder, hail, fire darting to ground</b></li><li class=\"d0\">On man, cattle, <b>every herb</b>, every tree - none like it since Egypt a nation</li><li class=\"d0\">Only <b>Goshen</b> - no hail; split still made, but Egyptians got <b>extra warning</b> - if they believed</li></ul>"},{"t":857.6,"lv":3,"h":"Fire = lightning","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Father Stephen ruins your Sunday school\": <b>fire is lightning</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Egypt: almost <b>no rain</b> - they called rain <b>\"Niles in the sky\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Thunder, lightning, <b>massive hailstones</b></li><li class=\"d0\">No concept of electricity → lightning = <b>\"fire from heaven\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">lightning strike catches things on fire - makes sense</li></ul>"},{"t":932.58,"lv":2,"h":"9:27-35 - \"I have sinned this time\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh sends for Moses and Aaron: <b>\"I have sinned this time. The Lord is righteous, my people and I are ungodly\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">notice <b>\"this time\"</b> - the others weren't his fault</li><li class=\"d1\">\"should have listened and brought everyone inside - <b>my bad</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not getting it at all\" - can't acknowledge what's happening</li><li class=\"d0\">Pray for me, end thunder and hail → <b>I will let you go</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: when I'm out of the city I'll spread my hands - <b>earth is the Lord's</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><i>eretz</i> = earth <b>or land</b> - likelier <b>land</b>: the whole of Egypt belongs to <b>Yahweh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Moses: \"you don't really get it\" - <b>\"fool me once\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Crops: <b>flax, barley</b> struck; <b>wheat, rye</b> late, spared</li><li class=\"d1\">food problems on top of dead people</li><li class=\"d0\">Storm stops → Pharaoh <b>sinned yet more</b>, hardened his heart <b>and his servants'</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"just like Moses said, because God told him\" - <b>pattern recognition</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1089.4,"lv":2,"h":"Exodus 10:1-2 - Hardening of the heart","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 10</b> - \"for <b>I</b> have hardened his heart and his servants'\"</li><li class=\"d1\">purpose: signs so you tell <b>children and children's children</b> how I <b>mocked the Egyptians</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"Another sorry Calvinist\" - people get hung up</li><li class=\"d1\">two verses ago: <b>Pharaoh</b> hardened his own heart - and <b>his servants' hearts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to read it as God forcing, Pharaoh must have power into servants' hearts - \"maybe hypnosis\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Hardening of heart</b> = weighed down by <b>evil, sin, wickedness</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God sees it full of sin; doesn't say God <b>made</b> him sin</li><li class=\"d1\">God's involvement = <b>not forgiving him</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1192.04,"lv":3,"h":"Patience ends - Acts 17","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Before the last plague: \"up to this point I've been <b>patient</b>\" - that's about to change</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Paul in Athens, Acts 17</b>: up until now God hasn't <b>reckoned</b> your sins against you</li><li class=\"d1\">nations \"don't know any better\"; he's been letting you be</li><li class=\"d1\">now time is coming → <b>repent</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same thing said to Pharaoh</li><li class=\"d1\">up until that plague, patient; now Pharaoh's sin <b>held against him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God won't lighten his heart by <b>forgiving, bearing with</b> him</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Reckoning begun</b> in these final plagues</li><li class=\"d0\">Tell your children's children \"all the way down to today, in the year <b>2024</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1286.74,"lv":2,"h":"10:3-11 - Plague 8 warning: humble yourself","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v3: <b>\"How long will you refuse to humble yourself before me?\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>first time</b> that language - before: \"you <b>exalt</b> yourself against my people\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh: \"of course I'm better than your people, they're slaves\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh humbles himself to no one - maybe the <b>sun god</b>, his father; not the god of slaves</li><li class=\"d0\">Tomorrow <b>locusts</b> - cover the face of the earth, eat residue left from <b>hail</b>, every tree</li><li class=\"d1\">houses full - not seen <b>since humans have been on earth</b> (last one: since Egypt a nation)</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses leaves. Every warning has come true → \"<b>I can't eat gold, bro</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">but acknowledging = <b>humble himself</b>, admit the slaves' God <b>bested him</b> - \"requires too much\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Servants</b>: \"How long shall this man be a <b>snare</b> to us? Do you not yet know <b>Egypt is destroyed</b>?\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"We don't even like them. Just let them go, man\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses and Aaron called back: \"Go serve - but <b>who are the ones going</b>?\" - negotiating again</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses: young and old, sons and daughters, <b>sheep and oxen</b> - a <b>feast</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Pharaoh: <b>men only</b>; women, children, belongings stay - \"for evil lies before you\" → driven out</li></ul>"},{"t":1512.87,"lv":2,"h":"10:12-20 - Plague 8: locusts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v12: Moses stretches out rod → <b>south wind</b> all day and night → locusts</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Never been, never will be</b> a swarm like this</li><li class=\"d1\">cover the land, eat every herb and all fruit left by hail</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>nothing green</b> left in all Egypt</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh in haste: <b>\"I have sinned against the Lord your God and against you\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"Oh, I really blew it. <b>There's no food</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>pardon my sin</b> - \"take away from me this death\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses prays → <b>strong wind from the sea</b> blows locusts into the <b>Red Sea</b> - not one left</li><li class=\"d0\">But <b>the Lord hardened Pharaoh's heart</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1599.17,"lv":3,"h":"Repentance is not feeling bad","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Why \"Lord hardened\"? He asked <b>pardon</b> - <b>God did not pardon</b>; he still didn't let them go</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Repentance</b> is not feeling bad</li><li class=\"d1\">not disliking <b>consequences</b> and wanting off the hook</li><li class=\"d1\">= actually <b>changing</b> how you think, act, what you do</li><li class=\"d0\">God would forgive if he repented - the <b>sign</b> = he'd have <b>let them go</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"gosh, I feel bad, please forgive me, pray\" - <b>not repenting</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"God cares about what you <b>do</b>. God doesn't really care how you <b>feel</b>\" (shocks millennials)</li><li class=\"d1\">wrong thing + feel bad = still wrong; right thing, heart not in it = still right</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Parable of the two sons</b></li><li class=\"d1\">first: \"buzz off, dad\" - later <b>goes and works the vineyard</b>; not just feeling bad or apologizing for rudeness</li><li class=\"d1\">second: \"Yeah, I'm on it\" - polite, <b>doesn't do it</b></li><li class=\"d0\">God wants you to <b>confess</b>, then <b>work to change</b>, fix what you broke, <b>repair the damage</b></li><li class=\"d1\">begrudgingly - \"not ideal, but at least you're doing it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Society: don't do it if heart's not in it → <b>divorce rate</b></li><li class=\"d1\">leave family because heart's not in it vs. <b>stay and do the right thing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">morality through history = <b>doing the right thing</b>, not gratifying desires</li><li class=\"d1\">now \"follow your heart\" - at judgment before Christ: \"I pursued happiness\"? - <b>not weighed before an alligator god</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1836.88,"lv":2,"h":"10:21-23 - Plague 9: darkness","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Plague nine</b> - king of the gods for Egypt = <b>Ra, the sun god</b></li><li class=\"d0\">v21: darkness <b>that may be felt</b> - three days; <b>no one saw his brother</b>, no one rose from bed</li><li class=\"d0\">Israel <b>had light in their dwellings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just no sun: <b>can't light a fire, candle, lamp</b> - pitch black, except <b>Goshen</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Right in the face of <b>Ra</b> - can't get through the darkness <b>Yahweh</b> causes</li><li class=\"d0\">Pitch black: his first time on a <b>camping trip in the desert</b> (grew up in California)</li><li class=\"d1\">flashlights off - <b>hand two inches from face</b>, couldn't see it</li><li class=\"d0\">Seems no escalation - imagine <b>everyone blind</b> for three days: no work, no food, no water</li></ul>"},{"t":1960.83,"lv":2,"h":"10:24-29 - Pharaoh's last negotiation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">v24: \"Go serve the Lord - only sheep and oxen <b>kept back</b>; little ones may go\"</li><li class=\"d1\">still <b>negotiating</b> - still puts himself on a <b>par with Yahweh</b>, where he doesn't have to obey</li><li class=\"d0\">Moses: <b>no</b> - you must give us <b>burnt offerings and sacrifices</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not a hoof left behind</b>; we don't know how we'll serve <b>until we arrive</b></li><li class=\"d1\">worship = <b>sacrifice</b> in the ancient world</li><li class=\"d0\">v27: <b>Lord hardened</b> Pharaoh's heart</li><li class=\"d0\">Pharaoh: <b>\"Depart from me... in the day you see my face you shall die\"</b> - a threat</li><li class=\"d1\">Moses: \"You have spoken well, I will never see your face again\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Okay, take your animals\" → \"Nope, get away... I'm gonna kill you\" - <b>\"that ain't repentance\"</b> → no forgiveness</li></ul>"},{"t":2048.37,"lv":3,"h":"Why Pharaoh can't turn","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pushed to the edge of what's next week: <b>\"true horror\"</b> - \"this wasn't... compared to what's gonna happen\"</li><li class=\"d0\">He <b>cannot make the mental turn</b>: someone or something in the universe I <b>have to obey</b></li><li class=\"d1\">even <b>advisors</b> see it</li><li class=\"d1\">not that he can't see it - <b>can't accept</b> it: requires <b>too much</b>, his whole <b>cosmology</b>, sense of the world</li><li class=\"d0\">Why coming on him? <b>Mass murder of infants</b>, <b>enslavement</b> of a whole people group</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not some poor random guy\"; God's given him a <b>free ride</b></li><li class=\"d1\">in position to <b>bring order</b> - should have governed justly</li><li class=\"d1\">could have stopped at plague one, or <b>before Moses first showed up</b> - \"let us go sacrifice, couple days in the desert\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Now it's going to get <b>really bad</b> - but God will also <b>reveal himself</b> in a powerful way</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next week: <b>\"true horror\"</b> - more on God revealing himself"});
